# SYNOPSIS

```usage
vxfs mkfs [-u user] image mib branch ...
vxfs put image branch dir
vxfs ls image label [path]
vxfs cat image label path
vxfs verify image label dir
vxfs check image
vxfs info image
vxfs snap image branch label
vxfs fork image label branch
vxfs del image label
vxfs rollback image branch label
```

# DESCRIPTION

`vxfs` makes, fills, reads and checks images of vx-fs volumes (see vxfs(6)) on the development machine, with `lib/vx-fs`, the library fsd(4) uses.
An image is an ordinary file holding the volume, as a partition would.
build(1) uses it to make the volumes its test scenarios boot with, and its `check` makes one, fills it and checks it.

A <label> names a tree: a snapshot's label, or a branch's name, which means the branch's last commit.
Each command that changes the volume does all its work, then commits once; if it fails before then, the volume is as its last commit left it.
The commands:

: `mkfs` [`-u` <user>] <image> <mib> <branch> ...
  Make <image> a new volume of <mib> MiB, 1 to 4194304, replacing whatever the file held, with each <branch> given an empty root directory, mode 0755, owned by user 0.
  If one branch is `adm`, its root gets `users`, the users file (see users(6)) as gefs writes it: `adm`, user 0, whose group holds <user>; `none`, user 1; and <user>, user 1000, `vectra` unless `-u` names another.
  If one branch is also `home`, its root is given to user 1000.
: `put` <image> <branch> <dir>
  Copy the host tree under <dir> into the root of <branch>: directories, regular files and symbolic links, with their permission bits and modification times, each owned by the branch root's owner and group.
  Devices, sockets and FIFOs are skipped.
  It prints how many bytes of files it copied.
: `ls` <image> <label> [<path>]
  List a directory of the tree, `/` by default: for each entry a line of its kind (`d` a directory, `L` a symbolic link, `-` a file) and permission bits in octal, its owner's id, its length and its name, in the directory's order.
: `cat` <image> <label> <path>
  Write a file's contents to standard output.
: `verify` <image> <label> <dir>
  Compare the tree with the host tree under <dir>: the same names, kinds and link targets, and for each file the same permission bits, modification time and bytes, with nothing else in either.
  It names each host path that differs, and exits with status 0 only if none does.
: `check` <image>
  Run the volume checker: every snapshot, label and deadlist, and every block's allocation.
  It prints what it counted; on a volume that is not clean it prints `NOT CLEAN:` and the blocks leaked, unallocated, shared or damaged, and the bad snapshots and deadlists, and exits with status 1.
: `info` <image>
  Print the last commit's number, the arenas and the next generation, the space used, and each label, saying whether it is a branch, with its snapshot.
: `snap` <image> <branch> <label>
  Label the branch's last commit <label>, read-only.
: `fork` <image> <label> <branch>
  Make <branch>, a new branch whose tree starts as <label>'s.
: `del` <image> <label>
  Delete a label or a branch.
: `rollback` <image> <branch> <label>
  Set <branch> back to <label>'s tree.

`snap`, `fork`, `del` and `rollback` are the commands of the volume's `/adm/ctl` in fsd(4), done on an image.

# EXAMPLES

A volume with the system volume's four branches, a tree put in `home`, a snapshot, and a look at it:

```rc
% vxfs mkfs v.img 64 store cfg home adm
% vxfs put v.img home t
vxfs: 6 bytes into home
% vxfs ls v.img home
d0755 1000          0 notes
% vxfs ls v.img adm
-0664    0         46 users
% vxfs cat v.img home /notes/hello.txt
hello
% vxfs snap v.img home home@1
% vxfs info v.img
commit 5, 1 arenas, next generation 19
used 112 of 65472 KiB
branch adm: snapshot 14
branch cfg: snapshot 8
branch home: snapshot 17
label home@1: snapshot 17
branch store: snapshot 7
% vxfs check v.img
4 snapshots, 5 labels, 0 deadlists; 7 blocks in use: 5 in trees, 2 else
% vxfs verify v.img home@1 t
```

build(1) is the usual caller: it runs `vxfs` from `out/host/vxfs`, which it builds from source when the source has changed.

# FILES

: `out/host/vxfs`
  The program, as build(1) builds it.
: `out/vxfs/check.img`
  The image build(1)'s `check` makes, and its log beside it.

# SEE ALSO

build(1), fsd(4), vxfs(6), users(6), vxstore(8)

# DIAGNOSTICS

A failure prints `vxfs:` and what failed, with the library's status number when there is one, such as `vxfs: no label home@2: status -15`, and exits with status 1.
A command it does not know, or the wrong number of arguments, prints its own usage message, which spells the parameters in capitals, and exits with status 2.

# BUGS

`put` cannot replace: a name the branch's root already holds makes it fail, so it fills only directories that do not yet have what it copies.
Hard links are copied as separate files, and the host's owners are not kept.
`verify` compares the permission bits and times of files, but not of directories.
